  "summary": [
    "Batch B, family B1 (`path_vertices`). Nine conjecture-local helpers now unfold to `GTBase.walks_paths.seq_vertices`, MathComp's support `[set:: s]` of a raw vertex sequence: eight are the comprehension `[set v | v \\in p]` (X67 writes `[set x : G | x \\in p]`), and Digraph X2's `x2_path_vertices x s`, the support of the head-plus-tail sequence `x :: s`, keeps its signature as `seq_vertices (x :: s)`. The canonical has no walk, uniqueness or nonemptiness premise; `seq_vertices_nodes` and `seq_vertices_val` state its exact correspondence with coq-graph-theory's packaged `Path`, whose `nodes` is the head-plus-tail list. Every helper is convertible to the canonical, so each certificate is a kernel-checked conversion, the helper ones going through `seq_verticesE`; `meta/check_library_migration.py` checks Print Assumptions.",
    "",
    "Fourteen statements are affected: X3, X2 (three rows), X39, X113, X116, X146, X11, X67 and X26 in the helpers' own files, and the cross-module rows X40 (through X39's `x39_has_k_distant_xy_paths` and `x39_separates_xy`), X52 and X90 (through X2's `contains_subdivision`). Each frozen statement resolves through frozen copies along its whole affected chain: the helpers in `Legacy`, prefix-dropped chain copies in per-row `XnnLegacy` modules, and X2's unprefixed chain in dependency-ordered modules (`X2Legacy`, `X2BoundsLegacy`, `X2MaderianLegacy`, then one statement module per X2 row), so that every reference to a frozen declaration is renamed or module-qualified. `x2_path_vertices` and `x2_path_internal` are frozen inside verbatim copies of their `Section SubdivisionModel` scaffolding, so their discharged arguments are unchanged. Declarations outside the chains resolve through their live definitions, which this migration does not change.",
    "",
    "Kernel evidence, independent of this textual report: `Print All Dependencies` of the 14 frozen statements contains no live helper, no live chain declaration and not `seq_vertices`, while each of the 14 live statements contains `seq_vertices` and its alias (/srv/graph-theory-rocq/coordination/evidence/B1-path_vertices/print_all_dependencies_summary.txt, with the probe script and the full output beside it). The Section scaffolding lines of the frozen X2 copies are checked verbatim against the baseline in /srv/graph-theory-rocq/coordination/evidence/B1-path_vertices/section_scaffolding.txt.",
    "",
    "No statement text, doc block, manifest row or leg state changes (checked below), so the documented discrepancies of the affected rows stay verbatim: the wave-E4 nonemptiness guards of the X2 Mader bounds and of X52, the LEAST clause of X2's Mader row and its candidate edge e173, the solved status of X52 and X67, the partial status of X40, X26's d = 0 degeneration, X11's k = 0 behaviour, and the affirmative reading of the X3 question row. The same-body helpers of later families (`vertices_of_seq`, `cycle_vertices`) are untouched distinct variants below; the `path_internal` companions are migrated by family internal-vertices (B2)."
  ],
